  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Energy obligated $593M in FY2027 to date. The agency recorded 157 awards with an average award size of $3.8M. Obligations fell 98.9% year over year, and current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date). Historical context shows much larger full-year totals in recent years: FY22 obligations were $41.2B, FY23 obligations were $44.6B, FY24 obligations were $46B, FY25 obligations were $48.5B, and FY26 obligations were $55.1B. This snapshot reflects the early, partial nature of FY2027 contracting activity compared with prior full fiscal years.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How much has the Department of Energy obligated so far this fiscal year?",
        "body": "The Department of Energy obligated $593M in FY2027 to date. The Department of Energy recorded 157 awards with an average award size of $3.8M. Obligations fell 98.9% year over year. Current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date)."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are Energy's top contract categories and largest vendors in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) is the largest category at $398M. Hazardous Waste Treatment and Disposal is $100M, and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences is $81.1M. FLUOR MARINE PROPULSION, LLC is the largest vendor at $373M, followed by HANFORD TANK WASTE OPERATIONS & CLOSURE, LLC at $100M, and UCHICAGO ARGONNE, LLC at $81.1M."
      }
    ]
  },
